  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "The huaconada is the ritual dance of Mito in Concepción province, Junín, performed in the first days of January and inscribed by UNESCO in 2010, in which masked men called huacones, carrying whips, dance through the plaza as guardians of communal order. Their stately, swaggering steps are played by the Mantaro orquesta típica of clarinets, saxophones, violin and harp.",
